cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PotatoClaw in research or experiments, please cite this repository."
title: "PotatoClaw: Ultra-Low-Resource Local AI Computer Agent"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kanth"
    given-names: "Chaman Prakash"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChamanPrakashKanth/potatoclaw"
url: "https://github.com/ChamanPrakashKanth/potatoclaw"
abstract: >-
  PotatoClaw is an experimental local AI computer-agent framework for budget
  hardware. It combines small local language models with deterministic graph
  planning, bounded working memory, concept-graph memory experiments, tool use,
  execution verification, and failure-aware control to study useful autonomous
  behavior under tight VRAM and context constraints.
keywords:
  - "local AI agent"
  - "computer use agent"
  - "small language model"
  - "4GB VRAM"
  - "bounded working memory"
  - "concept graph memory"
  - "BMW memory"
  - "deterministic verification"
  - "llama.cpp"
  - "offline AI"
